<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The window background, which is what shows through before and around
  anything Compose paints.

  This was android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar, which is why the settings
  screen was white: MolassesTheme sets Compose colours but not the window, and
  the launcher only looked correct because it wraps itself in a Surface that
  covers the window entirely. SettingsActivity does not, so the platform theme
  showed through.

  Black rather than a token from Color.kt because this is resolved by the
  platform before any Compose code runs. The two must be kept in step by hand;
  JitterBackground is 0xFF000000 for exactly this reason.

  ## statusBarColor and navigationBarColor do nothing on Android 15

  They are kept, and they are not what is making the bars black on a modern
  device. Window.setStatusBarColor and setNavigationBarColor are both
  deprecated, and both carry the same sentence: if the app targets
  VANILLA_ICE_CREAM (API 35) or above, the colour will be transparent and
  cannot be changed. targetSdk is 35, so on Android 15 and later these two
  lines are read and discarded.

  They are still honoured on API 30 to 34, which minSdk 30 includes, so
  deleting them would change the bars on every device below 15 to whatever
  Theme.Material.NoActionBar defaults to. That is why they stay.

  On 15 and later the bars are black for a different reason: the bar
  backgrounds are transparent, both activities fill the window with a Surface
  coloured JitterBackground, and JitterBackground is 0xFF000000. That is the
  hand-kept pairing the note above describes, and on 15 it is the only thing
  doing the work. A reader who changes JitterBackground and expects these two
  lines to hold the bars will be wrong on every device that matters.

  ## windowLightStatusBar is declared rather than defaulted

  Unset, it defaults to false, which means light icons, which is correct on
  black. That is correct by luck rather than by statement, and it stops being
  correct on the first screen with a light background. Declared, the pairing
  with the black window background is visible in one place, and a future light
  theme has to change it deliberately.

  windowLightNavigationBar is set for the same reason. Leaving it implicit
  while fixing its neighbour would reproduce the exact fault being fixed.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Molasses" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/black</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightNavigationBar">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>
